⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of The Dual-Vector Foil
node DVF · DVF · ⟦The Dual-Vector Foil:DVF:1a3e1b⟧

WHO   — The Dual-Vector Foil — death by art — collapsing 3D space into 2D
WHAT  — A dark-forest weapon: a small slip of material that initiates a runaway collapse of three-dimensional space into two dimensions. An unknown civilization flicks one into the Solar System, flattening the Sun and planets into a beautiful, lethal plane — the casual execution of a star system as a work of art.
WHERE — 3BT · The Technologia of Trisolaris  Framework inputs: Remembrance of Earth's Past + adaptations; real-science verdict  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — The dual-vector foil and the two-dimensionalization of the Solar System are the climax of Death's End — book three only. Neither live-action series has reached it yet, which makes it the purest 'on the page' marvel of the universe.
HOW   — FLUFF — and gorgeous. There is no known mechanism to lower a region of space out of a dimension. It rhymes loosely with real speculative ideas (extra spatial dimensions in string theory; false-vacuum decay as a cosmic phase change), but as written it is pure science fiction. Distinct from the photoid — that one is a kinetic star-killer; this one is a change to the rules of space itself.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  I am not a bomb. I am a lowering — I fold your three dimensions down to two and turn your whole world into a painting of itself.

